Let me put it this way: You're not wrong. It's perfectly fine to use {le}
instead of {lo}, but I wouldn't myself say it's better to. I also wouldn't
say it's worse to.

As long as the thing you're talking about can be the x1 of whatever you're
using to describe it (i.e. something you are calling {lo ve klama} must be
a means of transportation), {lo} is never wrong, so when in doubt, use {lo}=
.


